@verbs consent consents consentir
@tier player
@title deciding what others may do to you

There are things another player cannot do to you unless you allow
them. Each of those is a consent, set to yes or no, and every one
of them starts at no.

  consent                      lists how you have them now.
  consent <name> yes           allows it.
  consent <name> no            stops allowing it.

The consents, by the names you type, are:

  give        somebody giving you an object.
  protect     somebody protecting you in a fight.
  groups      being taken into an adventuring party.
  drinks      being bought a drink.
  autoequip   equipping yourself on entering the game.
  follow      somebody following you.
  raise       somebody bringing you back to life.

Anybody trying something you do not consent to is refused. With
'give', on top of that, you are told they tried.
